# Emet-Selch, Unsundered: "At the beginning of your upkeep, if there are fourteen or more cards in your graveyard, you may transform Emet-Selch." Turn 1 Bot1 casts it (the loot
# puts an Island in its graveyard). On turn 3 two Ancestral Recalls, a Breaking (mill eight) and a sacrificed Black Lotus make exactly fourteen cards in its graveyard once the
# attack's loot has discarded one more. It accepts at the turn 5 upkeep and Hades, Sorcerer of Eld (6/6) is there: "During your turn, you may play cards from your graveyard" - a Black Lotus
